# C2P - Calliope to PyPSA
[As from June 2021, Version 0.7.0]

C2P is part of the [EnerPlanET](https://mygit.th-deg.de/s6et/enerplanet) backend. It reads [Calliope](https://calliope.readthedocs.io) results to compute power flows with [PyPSA](https://pypsa.readthedocs.io).

## Installation

1. (OPTIONAL/RECOMMENDED) Virtual Environment \
Create and run a new virtual environment (e.g. virtualenv, conda, ..).

2. (REQUIRED) Download C2P\
Download latest .whl file and change to its directory.

2. (REQUIRED) Install C2P using whl file  \
Use the package manager pip to install latest c2p-*.whl file (e.g. version [0.7.0](https://mygit.th-deg.de/s6et/c2p/-/blob/master/c2p-0.7.0-py3-none-any.whl)).

    ```bash
    pip install c2p-0.8.2-py3-none-any.whl
    ```

## Usage
For usage with [EnerPlanET](https://mygit.th-deg.de/s6et/enerplanet) also setup the [Docker Backend](https://mygit.th-deg.de/tcf_s6et/docker_webservice).
For simple usage download C2P [main.py](https://mygit.th-deg.de/s6et/c2p/-/blob/master/main.py). \
**path** requires a Calliope model following the structure in described in the [Input](#input) section.

### Run C2P
```bash
python main.py <path> 
```
### Run C2P with test data
For testing download the version compatible test data from [c2p/test_data](https://mygit.th-deg.de/s6et/c2p/-/tree/master/test_data).

```bash
python main.py ./test_data/v07/sim_1622009906
```

## Decription
Uses results of a Calliope model and its topology from EnerPlanET as INPUT and computes power flows with PyPSA as OUTPUT.

### Input
Requires the **path** to a Calliope Model containing the structure and files shown in the following example, whereby 'sim_1622009906' is the model_name containing the model_id '1622009906': 

```bash
.
└── sim_1622009906
    ├── config.json
    ├── model.yaml
    ├── results
    │   ├── results_carrier_con.csv
    │   └── results_carrier_prod.csv
    └── results.nc 
```
#### Description of files

- Net-Topology and PyPSA Settings
    - **config.json** from EnerPlanET
- Consumption and Production Values
    - CSV files
        - located in results/ 
        - generated with calliope model.to_csv(path)
        - If it exists, the NetCDF is (prefered) used instead of CSV files
        - Filename: 
            - **results_carrier_prod.csv** (default)
            - **results_carrier_con.csv** (default)
    - NetCDF file *(alternativ, instead of CSV)*
        - generated with calliope model.to_netcdf(path)
        - Filename: **results.nc<area>** (default)

### Output

- PyPSA Network (for usage see [PyPSA documentation](https://pypsa.readthedocs.io/en/latest/components.html))
    - Folder with CSV files (default)
    - HDF5, NetCDF (optional)
- Settings
    - CSV file (default)
- Power Flow Results
    - CSV file (default)
    - HDF5, Excel (optional)

```bash
.
└── sim_1622009906
    └── pypsa_output
        ├── csv_sim_1622009906
        │   ├── buses.csv
        │   ├── buses-p.csv
        │   ├── buses-q.csv
        │   ├── buses-v_ang.csv
        │   ├── buses-v_mag_pu.csv
        │   ├── csv_web
        │   │   ├── buses-p-t.csv
        │   │   ├── buses-q-t.csv
        │   │   ├── buses-v_ang-t.csv
        │   │   ├── buses-v_ang-t-grad.csv
        │   │   ├── buses-v_mag_pu-t.csv
        │   │   ├── generators-p_set-t.csv
        │   │   ├── generators-p-t.csv
        │   │   ├── generators-q-t.csv
        │   │   ├── lines-p0-t.csv
        │   │   ├── lines-p1-t.csv
        │   │   ├── lines-q0-t.csv
        │   │   ├── lines-q1-t.csv
        │   │   ├── loads-p_set-t.csv
        │   │   ├── loads-p-t.csv
        │   │   ├── transformers-p0-t.csv
        │   │   ├── transformers-p1-t.csv
        │   │   ├── transformers-q0-t.csv
        │   │   └── transformers-q1-t.csv
        │   ├── generators.csv
        │   ├── generators-p.csv
        │   ├── generators-p_set.csv
        │   ├── generators-q.csv
        │   ├── lines.csv
        │   ├── lines-p0.csv
        │   ├── lines-p1.csv
        │   ├── lines-q0.csv
        │   ├── lines-q1.csv
        │   ├── loads.csv
        │   ├── loads-p.csv
        │   ├── loads-p_set.csv
        │   ├── network.csv
        │   ├── snapshots.csv
        │   ├── transformers.csv
        │   ├── transformers-p0.csv
        │   ├── transformers-p1.csv
        │   ├── transformers-q0.csv
        │   └── transformers-q1.csv
        ├── pf_result.csv
        └── settings.csv
```

Note: If no trafos are used, there won't be transformers*.csv files.

## Tested
Only tested using
- settings in main.py
- reading from Calliope CSV output files
- Linux Python=3.6.13 and Python=3.9.0
- Windows Python=3.6.13
